startup_steps:
  - Read workspace.uai, .uai/totem.uai, .uai/taboo.uai, canonical memory, decision index, .uai/short-term-memory.uai, .uai/operations.uai, and .uai/test-plan.uai.
  - Verify authoritative root and branch, inspect status without reverting unknown work, fetch remote, and confirm protected tree boundaries.
  - Treat reports as advisory and follow reviewed wiki/ledger routes rather than raw prose. Use workspace.uai current_companion_truth for current source state; preserve earlier checkpoint claims as historical.
  - Preserve immutable failed operations and all campaign counters.

current_truth:
  nuget: Owner requires current NuGet publication. C54 records absent current package IDs, repairs false missing-package classification and removes the monitor opt-in in source. Read operations.uai and nuget-publication-current-review.json; authentication, default-branch workflow, full native/package verification and source-authority gates remain open. No package was published.
  static_seed_browser: C53 MiniModel commit 4b815cbb877a709e8d3060c2039c13e993c334eb passes 79 checks including real Edge CORS and six exact Apache fixture bodies. Public TLS/LiteSpeed, real composition installation and qualification remain unproven.
  cache_cleanup: C52 schedules one background cleanup after successful saved-model activation or a successful check with no active installation. Sixteen passes and a 60-second cancellation signal bound new work; issued mutations retain their lock until settled. Advanced diagnostics distinguish stopping/incomplete from complete and count completed passes only. All 378 affected checks and 27 Edge tests pass; see startup-composition-cleanup-review.json. Empty cleanup creates no model root; cache/activation failures suppress it. No real-model/public gate passed.
  cache_retirement: C51 keeps external canonical staging authority until retired-directory absence is observed, reserving the active activation ID. All 369 affected checks, nine Edge tests and twelve smoke observations pass; two new Edge tests close a tab at terminal removal and resume bounded cleanup in a fresh tab. See composition-retirement-recovery-review.json. C52 adds startup scheduling; stalled mutations, power-loss durability and real-model/public gates remain separate limits.
  cache_startup: C50 gives startup cache verification one 60-second deadline. Open is read-only and OPFS root resolution is independent per operation. Timeout rejects late completion, releases the lock and shows recovery text; cache errors suppress automatic replacement pending explicit user action. Empty-cache bootstrap remains. All 336 affected checks, nineteen Edge tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass; see startup-cache-lifetime-review.json. Real-model timing, durable mutation/crash lifecycle and model/public gates remain open.
  cache_read_cancellation: C49 propagates supplied signals through metadata/member acquisition, metadata streams/hashes, enumeration and candidate validation. Cancellation remains distinct from corrupt data; pointer commit/readback still reconciles. See composition-read-cancellation-review.json. C50 supplies startup's signal; general signal-free calls, durable mutations and terminal orphan cleanup retain their separate lifetime limits.
  cache_readers: C48 gives each composition shared read leases and exclusive write/retirement locks. The app pins all six cached files through worker activation; companion validation requires withRead. Scope cleanup and cancellation release readers; actual Edge tabs prove waiting and release on closure. See composition-read-lease-review.json. Remaining crash/metadata lifetime and real model/public gates stay open.
  cache_ownership: C47 rejects unknown staging/installed content, bounds ownership inventories and removes only recognized direct files. Recovery keeps invalid pointer authority until content deletion succeeds; failed candidates keep markers on failed cleanup. All 143 affected checks, three Edge storage tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass; see composition-cleanup-ownership-review.json. Reader/crash lifecycle and real model/public gates remain open.
  cache_cancellation: C46 fixes a stalled source-cleanup wait that ignored later cancellation. All 118 affected checks, two Edge OPFS/cache tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass. Previous installation and lock availability are preserved; supplied signals are required. See composition-cleanup-cancellation-review.json. Whole-cache review and real model/public gates remain open.
  release_smoke: C45 v8 retains raw abort events and separately attributes only exact HTTP 200 probe bodies after independent byte verification. Minimal-page trials reproduced the distinction; bounded terminal-event waits replace a stalled Playwright response wait. All 34 smoke and 42 unchanged runtime checks plus the normal CLI pass. See completed-runtime-probe-review.json; no real model or public result.
  runtime_lifetime: C43 defers runtime download until a model operation, adds one 60-second deadline and cancellation through the shared admission/runtime helper, and reserves activation ownership before waiting. 262 focused, 26 artifact/publication and 14 Edge chooser checks pass. See browser-runtime-lifetime-review.json; model/public gates remain open.
  runtime_bytes: C42 bounds decoded runtime downloads before allocation/copy and moves build checks into owned canonical artifacts. All 48 checks pass; two offline builds exactly reproduce the tracked WASM after binding virtual profile mapping. See browser-runtime-streaming-review.json. No promotion, real model or public result.
  admission_lifetime: C41 gives browser qualification/admission checks one 30-second deadline plus explicit cancellation. 218 JavaScript and eight installed-Edge fixture checks pass; see admission-lifetime-review.json. Real-model/public gates remain open.
  companion: Production source acquisition, exclusive operation ownership, contained conversion, terminal reconciliation, six-member transfer, and listener wiring are implemented; Available is not model qualification.
  blocker: No authorized real-source acquisition receipt through this coordinator or qualified real model is established by the implementation and fixture evidence.
  browser: Current worktree product UI loads the capability client and composition installer; source wiring is not real-model browser or deployment proof.
  next_gate: Use the reviewed five-experiment plan; establish eligible source usefulness, fresh current v3 material registration and real native/WASM/browser evidence. Discover hosting capabilities independently; no replay of closed operations.
  candidate_gate: C39 retires the incompatible Qwen-only v1 producer; supported-profile discovery is the sole current v2 owner, with corrected access flags. Forty-five affected checks pass, retaining C35-C38 exclusions, bounds and owned receipts. Independent admission and real model gates remain; no-match is not admission.
  task_screen: C40 retires three superseded evaluators and old generator; useful checks now exercise v4/generator v2. All 17 frozen records remain unchanged and closed; 20 affected checks pass. See current-task-screen-review.json; no real model or new execution authority.
  current_state_details: workspace.uai
